-- title:
--   Arbitrary bounded predictable stopped original source Taylor jump sum is L¹ with expectation the exact Lévy-generator drift
-- statement:
--   On the original source probability space and its right-continuous predictable filtration, any bounded predictable weight a supported by the finite time horizon—including the random-stop discount a(t,ω)=exp(-qt)1_{t≤τ06(ω)}—yields an integrable literal controlled prepayment C² Taylor source-jump reward. Under explicitly stated genuine source future rectangle intensity hFuture and finite-band occupation, its expectation is exactly the finite physical μ-clock integral of a times the true spectrally negative Lévy generatorIntegrand negative-mark section, with inclusive ruinTime, negative extension of w and interior localization. No generic clock is incorrectly identified as the actual source jump compensator, and no automatic first source moment is assumed.
